      "id": "persian-fire-s015-p00772",
      "source_en": "Aristogiton. Following the establishment of democracy in Athens, a bronze of the tyrannicides—of which this is a Roman copy—was the only public portrait to be seen in the whole of the city. A squalid crime of passion had been transfigured into a heroic blow struck for liberty. (Museo Archeologico Nazionale, Naples/Bridgeman Art Library)",
